ENTRY            C3138   20260807   20261014   20261014       C259
SUBENT        C3138001   20260807   20261014   20261014       C259
BIB                 11         40
TITLE      Investigation of the isoscalar monopole response in
           the proton-rich nucleus 14O
AUTHOR     (J.C.Zamora,S.Giraud,R.G.T.Zegers,Y.Ayyad,
           S.Beceiro-Novo,D.Bazin,A.Carls,J.Chen,M.Cortesi,
           M.DeNudt,Yu-Gang Ma,C.Maher,W.Mittig,F.Ndayisabye,
           S.Noji,J.Pereira,A.Ravlic,J.Schmitt,M.Z.Serikow,
           L.J.Sun,J.Surbrook,N.Watwood,T.Wheeler,Z.Rahman,
           B.Zhou)
REFERENCE  (J,PL/B,879,140593,2026)
           #doi:10.1016/j.physletb.2026.140593
INSTITUTE  (1USAMSU,1USAANL,3CPRFUD,3CROZAG)
           (2SPNSPN) Universidade da Coruna, Campus Industrial de
           Ferrol, CITENI, Departamento de Fisica, Ferrol, 15403,
           Spain
FACILITY   (CYCLO,1USAMSU) The Coupled Cyclotron Facility of the
           National Superconducting Cyclotron Laboratory (NSCL).
INC-SOURCE A secondary 14O beam was produced by fragmentation of
           a 150 MeV/u 16O primary beam from the NSCL Coupled
           Cyclotron Facility (CCF) on a 1316 mg/cm2 thick 9Be
           production target placed at the entrance of the A1900
           fragment separator. A 70%-pure 105 MeV/u 14O beam with
           an intensity ranging from 200 to 700 kpps was generated
            by using a 150-mg/cm2 thick Al degrader in the A1900
           fragment separator. The main contaminants were 13N
           and 12C, accounting for 23% and 7%, respectively.
DETECTOR   (TPC,MAGSP) The AT-TPC (Active-Target Time Projection
           Chamber) was filled with pure deuterium gas at a
           pressure of 530 Torr.
METHOD     (TOF) The time-of-flight (ToF) between two
           scintillators located at the exit of the A1900 and
           the entrance of the S800 spectrograph beam line (S800
           object point) was used to separate the 14O beam from
           the contaminants on an event-by-event basis. The beam
           was transported achromatically to the AT-TPC installed
           at the pivot point of the S800 spectrograph.
CORRECTION Corrections for efficiency and acceptance were
           implemented through simulations using the ATTPCROOT
           analysis and simulation package.
STATUS     (APRVD) Approved by J.C.Zamora on August 15, 2026.
HISTORY    (20260807C) BP
ENDBIB              40
COMMON               1          3
EN
MEV/A
      105.0
ENDCOMMON            3
ENDSUBENT           47
SUBENT        C3138002   20260807   20261014   20261014       C259
BIB                  4         15
REACTION   (8-O-14(D,INL)8-O-14,ICL,DA/DE,D/RSD)
ANALYSIS   The double differential cross section was
           reconstructed for scattering angles of 3-6 degrees
           and excitation energies up to 26 MeV. A resolution of
           2.1 MeV full width at half maximum (FWHM) was
           achieved for the reconstructed excitation energy.
           Total cross section resulting from the sum of the two
           settings (13N and 12C fragments). The random
           coincidences were subtracted.
ERR-ANALYS (DATA-ERR) The error bars in the data include
           statistical and systematic uncertainties. The latter
           are dominated by the uncertainties in the beam
           intensity normalization and the acceptance correction.
STATUS     (TABLE,,J.C.Zamora+,J,PL/B,879,140593,2026) Fig. 2
           Data were provided by J.C.Zamora on August 8, 2026.
ENDBIB              15
